---
title: "112 Radiologic Science I - II"
code: "RAD-111"
category: "radiography"
credits: "4"
prerequisites:
  - "2026/RAD-105"
corequisites: []
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisites: RAD 105 and RAD 245"
---

Teaches concepts of radiation, radiography physics, fundamentals of electromagnetic radiation, electricity and magnetism, and application of these principles to radiography. Focus on x-ray production, emission, and x-ray interaction with matter. Lecture 3 hours, Laboratory 3 hour, Total 6 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
